{
  "id": "u08",
  "n": 8,
  "level": "A1",
  "title": "Reflexive verbs",
  "summary": "Daily routine: me levanto, me ducho, me acuesto.",
  "explain": [
    {"h": "Verbs that come with a pronoun"},
    {"p": "Reflexive verbs end in **-se** in the dictionary: *levantarse* (to get up). The action goes back to the person doing it. Conjugate the verb as usual and put the matching pronoun **before** it."},
    {"table": [["yo", "me levanto"], ["tú", "te levantas"], ["él / ella / usted", "se levanta"], ["nosotros", "nos levantamos"], ["vosotros", "os levantáis"], ["ellos / ustedes", "se levantan"]]},
    {"ex": ["Me levanto a las seis.", "I get up at six."]},
    {"ex": ["¿A qué hora te acuestas?", "What time do you go to bed?"]},
    {"p": "Common ones: **levantarse** (get up), **despertarse** (wake up, e→ie), **ducharse** (shower), **vestirse** (get dressed, e→i), **acostarse** (go to bed, o→ue), **llamarse** (be called), **quedarse** (stay), **sentarse** (sit down, e→ie), **irse** (leave)."},
    {"h": "With an infinitive"},
    {"p": "With *ir a*, *querer*, *poder*… the pronoun can go before the first verb **or** on the end of the infinitive. Both are correct:"},
    {"ex": ["Me voy a duchar. = Voy a ducharme.", "I'm going to have a shower."]},
    {"tip": "Negative: *no* comes before the pronoun: *No me acuerdo.* (I don't remember.)"}
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {"type": "table", "verb": "levantarse", "tags": ["forms"]},
    {"type": "table", "verb": "ducharse", "tags": ["forms"]},
    {"type": "gap", "q": "Yo ___ levanto a las seis.", "hint": "pronoun", "a": "me", "en": "I get up at six.", "tags": ["pronoun"]},
    {"type": "gap", "q": "¿A qué hora ___ acuestas?", "hint": "pronoun", "a": "te", "en": "What time do you go to bed?", "tags": ["pronoun"]},
    {"type": "gap", "q": "Mi jefe ___ llama Carlos.", "hint": "pronoun", "a": "se", "en": "My boss is called Carlos.", "tags": ["pronoun"]},
    {"type": "gap", "q": "Nosotros ___ quedamos en casa.", "hint": "pronoun", "a": "nos", "en": "We're staying at home.", "tags": ["pronoun"]},
    {"type": "gap", "q": "¿Vosotros ___ ducháis por la mañana?", "hint": "pronoun", "a": "os", "en": "Do you (all) shower in the morning?", "tags": ["pronoun"]},
    {"type": "gap", "q": "Yo me ___ a las siete.", "hint": "despertarse", "a": "despierto", "en": "I wake up at seven.", "tags": ["stem-change"]},
    {"type": "gap", "q": "Ellos se ___ tarde.", "hint": "acostarse", "a": "acuestan", "en": "They go to bed late.", "tags": ["stem-change"]},
    {"type": "gap", "q": "Me ___ rápido por la mañana.", "hint": "vestirse", "a": "visto", "en": "I get dressed quickly in the morning.", "tags": ["stem-change"]},
    {"type": "gap", "q": "¿Cómo te ___?", "hint": "llamarse", "a": "llamas", "en": "What's your name?", "tags": ["forms"]},
    {"type": "choice", "q": "Voy a ___ ahora.", "options": ["ducharme", "ducharse", "me ducho"], "a": 0, "why": "Pronoun on the infinitive matches the person: yo → ducharme.", "tags": ["infinitive"]},
    {"type": "choice", "q": "Nosotros ___ a las ocho.", "options": ["se levantan", "nos levantamos", "nos levantan"], "a": 1, "tags": ["pronoun", "forms"]},
    {"type": "choice", "q": "No ___ acuerdo.", "options": ["me", "yo"], "a": 0, "why": "No + pronoun + verb.", "tags": ["negative"]},
    {"type": "error", "q": "Yo levanto a las seis.", "a": "Yo me levanto a las seis.", "why": "Reflexive verbs need the pronoun.", "tags": ["pronoun"]},
    {"type": "error", "q": "Nosotros se quedamos aquí.", "a": "Nosotros nos quedamos aquí.", "why": "nosotros → nos.", "tags": ["pronoun"]},
    {"type": "error", "q": "Me no acuerdo.", "a": "No me acuerdo.", "why": "No goes before the pronoun.", "tags": ["negative"]},
    {"type": "transform", "instr": "Change to nosotros.", "q": "Me levanto temprano.", "a": "Nos levantamos temprano.", "tags": ["pronoun", "forms"]},
    {"type": "transform", "instr": "Say it another way (pronoun on the infinitive).", "q": "Me voy a sentar aquí.", "a": "Voy a sentarme aquí.", "tags": ["infinitive"]},
    {"type": "translate", "q": "I get up at seven.", "a": "Me levanto a las siete", "tags": ["forms"]},
    {"type": "translate", "q": "My name is Daniel.", "a": "Me llamo Daniel", "tags": ["forms"]},
    {"type": "translate", "q": "We are going to stay at home.", "a": "Vamos a quedarnos en casa / Nos vamos a quedar en casa", "tags": ["infinitive"]},
    {"type": "reorder", "words": ["Normalmente", "me", "acuesto", "a", "las", "once"], "a": "Normalmente me acuesto a las once", "en": "I usually go to bed at eleven.", "tags": ["stem-change"]},
    {"type": "reorder", "words": ["¿A", "qué", "hora", "os", "vais?"], "a": "¿A qué hora os vais?", "en": "What time are you (all) leaving?", "tags": ["pronoun"]}
  ]
}
